                I build the parts of a system that have to be correct under load — services, APIs and
                desktop clients that talk to real hardware — and I back them with tests.
            </p>

            <div class="skills-grid">
                <article class="card" data-reveal>
                    <div class="card-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-layers"></use></svg></div>
                    <h3>Backend &amp; APIs</h3>
                    <p class="proj-desc">
                        ASP.NET Core MVC services and RESTful APIs designed around SOLID and dependency
                        injection, with clean separation between transport, domain and persistence.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80">
                    <div class="card-icon"><svg class="icon"><use href="#i-code"></use></svg></div>
